 ['Sufi communities of Yemen','15th century','The first people we can document drinking coffee as a beverage, to stay awake for night prayers.'],
 ['Baba Budan','Sufi saint, c. 1670','Credited with bringing coffee to India by smuggling seven seeds out of Yemen.'],
 ['Pieter van den Broecke','Dutch trader, 1616','Took coffee plants from Mocha to Amsterdam, beginning European cultivation.'],
 ['Gabriel de Clieu','French naval officer, c. 1720','Carried a coffee seedling to Martinique, seeding Caribbean coffee.'],
 ['Francisco de Melo Palheta','Portuguese-Brazilian officer, 1727','Brought coffee to Brazil, the future giant of production.'],
 ['Erna Knutsen','Coffee importer, 1974','Coined "specialty coffee" to describe beans from special microclimates.'],
 ['The Peterson family','Hacienda La Esmeralda, 2004','Put Panama Geisha on the world stage and started the auction-record era.']
